* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.c text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.mm text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
# Patches must keep the byte layout they were generated with. The edk2 files they
# rewrite are stored with CRLF at the pin, and a patch whose context lines had their
# CRLF stripped no longer applies to them:
#
#   git apply --check  Usb-Bus.patch (CRLF)  onto UsbBus.h (CRLF)   -> applies
#   git apply --check  Usb-Bus.patch (LF)    onto UsbBus.h (CRLF)   -> patch does not apply
#
# So mark them -text: no end-of-line conversion on checkout or commit, in either
# direction. The -whitespace part stays so a console diff does not paint every line.
# scripts/check-patches-at-pin.py catches a regression here by applying the committed
# bytes to a tree fetched from the pin.
*.patch -text !eol -whitespace
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.efi binary
*.dtb binary
*.bin binary
*.a binary
*.o binary
